            <ArticleTitle>[Myocardial revascularization using Vineberg's procedure; 23 years follow-up].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1247-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors report the case of a patient followed up for 23 years after a double myocardial implantation of the internal mammary arteries (Vineberg technique) for unstable angina. The result of this procedure of surgical revascularisation has been very satisfactory to date. The authors believe this to be the longest follow-up reported in the medical literature.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
